            <div xml:id="d534">

                <pb facs="0513" n="503" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg503"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00B/3–2649: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-03-26T10:00:00+08:00">March 26, 1949—10
                            a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 26—4:23 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>655. Deptel 354, March 17. Military estimates [that] since September 1, 1948,
                    Communists have effectively integrated in own forces 210,000 troops which could
                    be used as combatant troops, including disaffected units and those surrendered
                    at Peiping. In addition Communists may have maximum of 400,000 captured
                    Nationalist troops being used as replacements or service forces.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
